Haro: libghostty-vt records Windows Terminal's win32-input-mode (DEC private mode 9001).

Pinned at ghostty 622b4ee. ConPTY asks the terminal for this mode at startup (microsoft/terminal
src/host/VtIo.cpp 201-203). Ghostty has no Windows frontend, so upstream has no entry for it. The
terminal only has to record the mode and report it to DECRQM; Haro encodes the keys itself
(src/keys/win32.ms).

diff --git a/src/terminal/modes.zig b/src/terminal/modes.zig
index ea35c8c..65cab90 100644
--- a/src/terminal/modes.zig
+++ b/src/terminal/modes.zig
@@ -390,6 +390,10 @@ const entries: []const ModeEntry = &.{
         // Kitty clipboard read that a paste event grants.
         .disabled = build_options.artifact != .lib and builtin.os.tag != .macos,
     },
+    // Windows Terminal win32-input-mode: ConPTY asks for each key as a
+    // KEY_EVENT_RECORD. The terminal only records it; the embedder encodes.
+    // See https://github.com/microsoft/terminal/blob/main/doc/specs/%234999%20-%20Improved%20keyboard%20handling%20in%20Conpty.md
+    .{ .name = "win32_input", .value = 9001 },
 };
 
